This aligns with expectations since these lower ion energies do not provide enough adatom mobility to produce surface diffusion for each added atom, resulting in short-range spatial features being replicated for subsequent layers. As the substrate bias voltage increases, the range in which the interface profile is vertically correlated between layers decreases. In other words, with higher ion energy, it becomes more difficult to replicate spatial features between subsequent layers. 

